## Core git workflow for b00t agents

| step | command | purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| 1 | `git checkout -b feat/<name>` | Create feature branch (never work on main) |
| 2 | `git add <files>` | Stage changes |
| 3 | `git commit -m "type(scope): message"` | Commit with conventional commit format |
| 4 | `git push origin feat/<name>` | Push branch |
| 5 | `gh pr create --fill` | Open PR (or `b00t checkpoint`) |
| 🦨 | `git push --force-with-lease` | ONLY for PR rebase — never on shared branches |

## Conventional commit format

Format: `type(scope): description`

```
feat(b00t-cli): add guard violation command
fix(hive): handle empty peer list
chore(deps): update ed25519-dalek to 2.2.0
docs(schema): add SCM-CONVENTIONS datum
refactor(hive): deduplicate peer store functions
```

## Branch naming

| prefix | purpose |
|--------|---------|
| feat/* | New features |
| fix/* | Bug fixes |
| chore/* | Maintenance |
| docs/* | Documentation |
| refactor/* | Code restructuring |
| experiment/* | Experimental (may be reverted) |

## b00t checkpoint shortcut

Instead of manual git commands, you can use:
```
b00t checkpoint       # git add -A + git commit + git push
b00t checkpoint --skip-tests   # skip test run during checkpoint
```

## 🦨 Pitfalls

- NEVER commit directly to main/dev — always branch first
- NEVER force-push without `--force-with-lease`
- ALWAYS run `cargo check` before committing
- Use `git status` before and after to verify state
- If rebase needed: use `git rebase main` NOT `git rebase origin/main`

## GGG checklist

Before opening a PR:
- [x] cargo check passes
- [x] cargo test --lib passes (or justified skip)
- [x] Branch name follows conventional format
- [x] Commit messages follow conventional format
- [x] No leftover merge conflict markers (<<<<<<<)
- [x] No debug println! or dbg! calls

